{"cluster_id": "C-1893", "topic": "The round budget implementation introduces no", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B048-036"], "canonical_claim": "The round-budget implementation introduces no persisted object kinds and no protocol-step changes; the budget is stack-local, and the one-pass round still commits `gc/state` exactly once.", "issue_ids": ["T6-1", "T6-2", "T6-3"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6b-review.md#L191-L209"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1894", "topic": "RefPlan changedRows and shouldDeferRound can defer", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B006-064", "B036-025", "B036-030", "B048-044"], "canonical_claim": "`RefPlan::changedRows` and `shouldDeferRound` can defer an entire fold round based on a listed tail observation, but the defer path performs no destructive work, advances no coverage cursor, and is bounded by `gc_fold_max_defer_rounds`. The DEFER decision is true exactly when changed-shard count is below `fold_threshold`, no destructive decision is due, and `rounds_since_last_fold` is below `gc_fold_max_defer_rounds`; otherwise the round FOLDs. The GC round DEFER mechanism bounds consecutive deferrals with `MaxDefer`; once the bound is reached, `GBegin` and weak fairness drive `GFold` so `unfolded` eventually returns to `{}`. FOLD and DEFER are mutually exclusive in an idle round: `DeferRound` is enabled only when `~GraduationDue` and its deferral condition hold, while `GBegin` is enabled for graduation or an exhausted honest defer budget.", "issue_ids": ["T7"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t7-laneA-review.md#L18-L76", "docs/superpowers/models/CaGcRoundDeferCore_RESULTS.md#modeling-decisions-assumptions", "docs/superpowers/models/CaGcRoundDeferCore_RESULTS.md#stage1-green", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-cas-gc-round-skip-unchanged-design.md#L52-L63"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1895", "topic": "The CaGcDestructiveGateCore model pins UniverseAuthoritative TRUE", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B048-050"], "canonical_claim": "The `CaGcDestructiveGateCore` model pins `UniverseAuthoritative == TRUE` because it models the post-flip posture; production's not-yet-knowable-universe posture suppresses destructive work and is covered by `CasGcFrontierGate.HiddenPlusOneInAnUnknownNamespaceIsRefusedByTheProductionDefault`.", "issue_ids": ["T6", "T7"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t7-laneB-report.md#L104-L112"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1896", "topic": "Normal rounds and healthy REBUILD apply", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B049-004"], "canonical_claim": "Normal rounds and healthy `REBUILD` apply every returned runtime retirement before downstream work and proceed only for `{Authoritative, DrainComplete}`; damaged-state `REBUILD` uses a no-parent, zero-catalog-mutation path.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75a-reconciler-report.md#scope"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1897", "topic": "The raw cas_gc_maintenance_state object at gc", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B049-014", "B049-015", "B049-083"], "canonical_claim": "The raw `cas_gc_maintenance_state` object at `gc/maintenance_state` stores only a bounded opaque janitor cursor and uses one materialized read followed by one expected-token or expected-absence CAS.; `cas_gc_maintenance_state` has no janitor invocation, `GcState`, fold, catalog, DEFER, or round-publication coupling.; No janitor state is stored in `gc/state` or a fold seal, and there is no lifecycle-specific cleanup attempt.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75d-maintenance-report.md#checkpoint-7-5d-gcmaintenancestate", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-step8-report.md#task-5-step-8-perpetual-namespace-janitor"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1898", "topic": "The maintenance state codec requires cur", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B049-016"], "canonical_claim": "The maintenance-state codec requires `cur`, limits decoded cursors to 64 KiB, uses `FormatId::GcMaintenanceState = 25` with `{7, 7}` change points, and caps raw control objects at 512 KiB.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75d-maintenance-report.md#checkpoint-7-5d-gcmaintenancestate"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1899", "topic": "Maintenance state CORRUPTED_DATA is classified as", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B049-017"], "canonical_claim": "Maintenance-state `CORRUPTED_DATA` is classified as corrupt with its exact token, while future-version and backend failures propagate; CAS conflicts do not retry, reread, or adopt a winner.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75d-maintenance-report.md#checkpoint-7-5d-gcmaintenancestate"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1900", "topic": "pre-fold catalog drain", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-024", "B049-043", "B049-044"], "canonical_claim": "The catalog-only pre-fold drain runs after lease acquisition against the authoritative adopted parent and before `DEFER`, the hot stream LIST, the successor catalog cut, fold, `REBUILD` adoption, or successor seal adoption. A pre-fold deletion requires the complete exact `Removing` row, matching parent cleanup evidence, and no durable hold. A GC invocation performs a catalog-only pre-fold drain after acquiring its lease and before defer, stream enumeration, the fold catalog cut, folding, or successor-seal adoption; it deletes only complete observed `Removing` rows whose matching adopted life row has cleanup evidence and no durable hold.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-prefold-amendment-report.md#decisions-implemented", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1901", "topic": "Full catalog tokens require a serial", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B049-046"], "canonical_claim": "Full-catalog tokens require a serial rescan after every CAS outcome; for `N` eligible rows the drain costs one adopted-seal GET, at least `N+1` complete catalog GETs, and `N` exact catalog CASes, plus retries for conflict or ambiguity.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-prefold-amendment-report.md#fix-round-1-5"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1902", "topic": "Healthy REBUILD drains before taking its", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B049-048"], "canonical_claim": "Healthy `REBUILD` drains before taking its fresh cut, while missing or undecodable `gc/state` adopts reconstructed authority only, performs zero catalog deletion, and leaves drain work to the next invocation.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-prefold-amendment-report.md#decisions-implemented"]}
