{"cluster_id": "C-1909", "topic": "janitor cursor advancement", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B049-076", "B049-078"], "canonical_claim": "A janitor page advances its cursor only when its catalog cut is unambiguous, deletion is globally admitted, and no candidate observes fence loss; suppressed, ambiguous, or fence-lost pages retain the old cursor for authoritative retry. Suppression, catalog ambiguity, and fence loss each retain the selected janitor page; fence loss stops subsequent deletes without rolling back earlier exact deletes, and a final fence recheck prevents progress after a retained-only page or authority loss following the last delete.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/task-5-step8-cpp-report.md#additional-step-8-pins", ".superpowers/sdd/task-5-step8-cpp-report.md#implemented-contract"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1910", "topic": "Malformed keys NotFound and exact token", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B049-077", "B049-081"], "canonical_claim": "Malformed keys, `NotFound`, and exact-token mismatch are decided per key and may advance the janitor page, while corrupt or backend-rejected cursor reset behavior remains exact-token based.; Corrupt or oversized janitor progress performs no LIST or delete and is reset only against its exact token; a backend-rejected cursor is likewise reset exactly before the error is surfaced, while cursor CAS conflicts are ignored.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-step8-report.md#task-5-step-8-perpetual-namespace-janitor", ".superpowers/sdd/task-5-step8-cpp-report.md#implemented-contract"]}
